# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Textbooks and anything derived from them never enter this repository.
#
# The copyright discipline is a property of the process, not the output, and the
# git history is the evidence for it. A repository that has never contained a
# textbook page cannot leak one, and that is provable years later in a way that
# "we were careful" is not. These rules exist from the first commit for that
# reason — do not relax them to make a one-off convenient.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The profiler's input folder. The profiler is the only tool permitted to read a
# textbook, and its input never gets committed.
bronne/

# Source documents of any kind. This catches CAPS documents too, which are
# public and which the planner is meant to read. They are still kept out, because
# the value of the rule above is that it is absolute: "this repo has never held a
# PDF" is checkable by anyone in one command, while "no PDFs except the approved
# ones" needs a human to audit which is which. CAPS is one download away, so the
# convenience it would buy is not worth weakening the only provable claim we have.
*.pdf
*.epub
*.djvu

# OCR intermediates. These now go to the scratch directory outside the repo, so
# anything matching here is an accident — which is exactly what should be caught.
*.tsv
*.hocr
*.png
*.ppm
*.pgm
*.pbm
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp

# Reading copies and the human-only working notes beside them. ALL generated, and
# never source: the PDFs rebuild from the lesson JSON in one command, and the notes
# duplicate reasoning that already lives in the specs and in the scripts' own comments.
#
# The reason this is a rule and not a preference: the heading dumps in here are OCR of
# real textbook pages -- full page text, which is how unit boundaries get found. They
# are marked FOR HUMAN EYES ONLY at the top of each file, but a marking is not a
# control. Committing them would break the one claim the rules above exist to protect,
# that this repository has never held a textbook page, and that claim is only worth
# anything while it is absolute.
lees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch and setup artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Claude Code discovers skills only under .claude/skills/. The canonical copy of
# the standard lives at skills/wolkskool-inhoudstandaard/ and this is a junction
# to it, created by bin/opstel.py. Committing it would duplicate every file.
.claude/skills/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editors and OS furniture
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
